Per-test classification provides diagnostic information (which specific tests fail) at no cost to variant-level accuracy. This parallels process supervision~\cite{lightman2023letsverify}: step-level verification enables error localization without accuracy loss.

Oracle analysis on SWE-bench Verified (500 instances) shows that per-test advantage concentrates at $T \geq 2$ fail-to-pass tests (31.3\% of instances, contributing 55.3\% of the total oracle advantage; Appendix~\ref{app:oracle}).


